/* NOTAREAL Wrestling moveset: every move is data: who it needs (situation), damage and momentum, frame timing, and the BODY MOVEMENT of both wrestlers
 * as pose keyframes (lean = tilt in degrees toward the opponent, lift = pixels off the mat, rot = full spin in degrees, sx/sy = squash/stretch,
 * dx = lunge in pixels, arm/leg = limb swing in degrees). The fight engine (nrfight.js) plays the poses frame by frame, so a suplex really lifts
 * and flips the victim, a clothesline is a running lunge with a stiff arm, and a top-rope splash climbs, leaps and lands flat.
 * The shapes follow the way pro-wrestling games (WWF No Mercy, WrestleMania 2000, SmackDown) structure a move list: strikes, grapples by facing
 * (front / back), running moves, ground moves, top-rope moves and signature finishers. Numbers are tuned feel, not measured from a ROM. */
